{
  "id": "cat-burglars",
  "type": "system",
  "title": "Nine Lives Gang",
  "description": "The Foundry VTT game system for Nine Lives Gang, a tabletop roleplaying game by Richard Moore: a gang of street cats robs a house. Automation-first: cat sheets, a roll dialog that knows who is watching, roll cards with Push, the two-meter Mood with Shoo! and Scooped!, and a Robbery Tracker that runs the house's turn (pets, noise, routines, Searching, the Prize Clock) and the outcome. Includes five ready-to-play games, one for each ready-to-run house: its map as a scene, its residents and the ready-made gang with their pictures, and a one-click quick start in the Robbery Tracker that sets the table and starts the robbery, with tokens that follow it round the house and on the getaway.",
  "version": "0.9.0",
  "compatibility": {
    "minimum": "13",
    "verified": "14"
  },
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Richard Moore",
      "url": "https://github.com/PainHog/CBZ"
    }
  ],
